---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { AUTHOR } from '../lib/author';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About CreatorForge"
  description="Who writes CreatorForge, how we evaluate tools, and how we handle affiliate links and recommendations."
>
  <div class="prose-article mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <h1>About CreatorForge</h1>
    <p>
      CreatorForge covers the AI tools YouTubers, Facebook and TikTok creators,
      designers, and small online businesses actually use — voice generation,
      AI video and image tools, automation, and the platforms built around them.
    </p>

    <h2>Who writes this</h2>
    <p>
      Articles are written and edited by <strong>{AUTHOR.name}</strong>,
      {AUTHOR.title.toLowerCase()}. {AUTHOR.bio}
    </p>

    <h2>How we evaluate tools</h2>
    <p>
      Not every article here is a hands-on lab test yet, and we'd rather say
      that plainly than imply otherwise. Right now, coverage falls into two
      categories:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Documentation-based comparisons</strong> — built from each
        provider's official pricing pages, API docs, and terms of service,
        cross-checked against each other rather than a single vendor's claims.
        These are marked as such where it matters (pricing, licensing, and
        commercial-use terms in particular change often, so we link the
        primary source instead of restating a number that can go stale).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Direct production experience</strong> — the AI voice, TTS
        chunking, and automation guidance on this site comes from running an
        actual narration/automation pipeline day to day, not from reading a
        changelog. Where an article describes a specific setting, failure
        mode, or workaround, that's something we've actually hit.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We're moving toward more structured, repeatable hands-on testing
      (same test script across competing tools, published cost/time/error
      results) — articles that include that will say so explicitly, with the
      test date and method next to the claim.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      Some links on this site are affiliate links. If you buy through one, we
      may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. Affiliate relationships
      never determine our recommendations — articles are marked when they
      contain affiliate links, and unverified claims are labeled as such
      rather than stated as fact.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Pricing, licensing, and platform policies change faster than any article
      can track perfectly. If something here is out of date or wrong, we'd
      rather know and fix it than leave it — tools and features can vary by
      country too, and we try to flag that rather than assume a US default
      applies everywhere.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
